**S2E09 — Potatopia researched (ASR-provisional):** [dossier](episodes/S2E09.md) · [full exact P/Q8 ASR comparison](../reports/DELVERS_S2E09_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md), **1,608 / 23,248 = 6.92% textual disagreement** (**not WER, verified accuracy**). Pinned `main` `bd23743219702ca258bd181a2e1999f4b3c9af48` confirmed via GitHub, complete Parakeet 00:00–03:04:11.150 and complete Q parsed with selected independent Q windows, no audio/GM handouts. **GM retrospectively resolves S2E08's unfinished fight:** red dragon **Fredoroth** killed by **Marsh's Arrow of Dragon Slaying**, **Evelyn's Forced Landing and Marsh's Sealed Gate activated**, **Skoogie survives**, dragon treasure split **3,000 gp each Koh/Krandal** but **Marsh carts away magic items**; **250 gp guild reward each**, **Krandal pockets extra 64 gp**; no proven equal item-value division. Guild encounter, party spends night apart; **minotaur skull actually named Chad**, farm hoard grows and Krandal retains 2,000 gp on person. **Marguerite reports red dragonborn with axe intruding Evelyn's dorm** (NPC report, source unknown), **all Delvers invited to Broscale dinner** two nights later. **Anthela/Anthila Spiros physically leaks black goo and Koh psychically witnesses coerced wedding to “Khalazar,” emperor of Lower Kingdoms**, ring briefly restores recognition but mind resets; no cure. Krandal feeds homeless **stranger with fluid-like back hump**, **actually gives 8 gp and a candle**, offers future 2 gp/job (not executed); stranger warns farm is vulnerable when darkness comes. **Koh gives Penelope red-dragon tooth and one-scale necklace**. Krandal catches fairy dragons causing guild's involuntary rhyming/psychic damage; Koh unaffected. **Cassius fears cult action at Bronze Ball** and promises Carrie research **day before ball**, only hypothesis/promise. **Koh + Krandal actually enter comatose Rianu Keeves's mental space** with Psychic Whispers; **Krandal casts Command and Lesser Restoration there, temporarily restoring Keeves's awareness but NOT waking body**, later Carrie **suggests Remove Curse, not cast**. **Krandal pays 50 gp for farm tools** at Grapple & Tackle; delivery pending. At **played Broscale Manor dinner** with Wildfire, Valentine, Climber, Basher, Dreamer, Wall Nibbler and Godwin Milner, Wildfire reviews guild reports and **grants recommendation for silver, not actual promotion**. **Privately tells Evelyn he knows she was in Withers's basement**, defends patron Withers; no public accusation, party leaves manor at **actual episode cutoff**. **Next bounded Delvers S2E10 — Carrie On**, present in [inventory](SOURCE_INVENTORY.md), unresearched. Listen for Fredoroth, Khalazar, wife/family spellings, sheriff-like warning stranger, actual loot/custody, guild signatories and silver rank status.

**S2E08 — Golden Potato Sword researched (ASR-provisional):** [dossier](episodes/S2E08.md) · [remote P/Q8 report](../reports/DELVERS_S2E08_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md), **1,986 / 24,378 = 8.15% exact textual disagreement** (**not WER/accuracy**); primary complete 00:00–02:56:46.070, entire Q parsed for metric and selected Q windows independently read, no sound. **Version caveat:** local checkout clean at `14c70f8be6772f0f7c7bd3e53fb8301da01e80d5`, GitHub cannot resolve that HEAD; remote default-branch source blob SHAs recorded, local first/end samples match but **whole-file equivalence not proven**. GM opening **retrospectively establishes Ambermoor has been delivered alive to guild holding cells and Delvers immediately sent with silver-ranked guest `Marsh` (played by Garrett)**, not an in-scene guild evidence debrief or payout. Marsh brings dragon-bone bow, scarred face and weasel **Wheatley**, leads **Dragon Mountain at Chath/Chaff Peak**; guild advertises ~100-year red dragon / 1,000 gp total, but at waterfall Marsh estimates **~450-year-old** giant dragon. Guild equips party in **temporary fire-resistant leather/chain/scale armor**; Krandal temporarily unattunes Staff of Python (held in Evelyn's bag). First dragon frightens three Delvers and **breathes 56 raw fire**, mitigated by fire resistance. Dragon captures three bound kobolds from village and eats them. **Skoogie**, kobold shaman seeking restored influence, **actually gives Marsh Arrow of Dragon Slaying**, not yet fired, and leads hidden lava-tube way. Marsh uses Jump; Krandal **solidifies crossing lava with Create Water**. Ancient **Radiant Lance** mechanism labels **Lava Off / Sealed Gate / Forced Landing** and tests freedom from greed; **Evelyn sacrifices ~250 gp plus Krandal's burnt potato**, receives **Dragon Slayer's Longsword**, **not potato composite**. Koh's ball bearings and Krandal's candles do not produce useful magical items. In **played lair combat**, Skoogie grants **10 temp HP**, Krandal **Aid +10 max/current HP**, Evelyn hits red dragon with sword crit **~37** and heals burning Skoogie. **Koh activates Lava Off**, creates thick **steam**. Marsh casts **Pass Without Trace** toward east gate, Evelyn heads to south forced-landing switch using Locate Object, **neither switch activated**; Krandal disperses small steam region and shelters in treasure cart **without looting**; dragon alive and airborne, combat **suspended mid-encounter** for guest scheduling. **No completion, reward, arrow hit, dragon kill or city return**. **Next bounded Delvers S2E09 — Potatopia** available in [inventory](SOURCE_INVENTORY.md), **unresearched**. Listen/check GM map, fire-resistance mechanics, age/names, arrow, sword and remote/local source identity.

**S2E07 — The Devils Eggs researched (ASR-provisional):** [dossier](episodes/S2E07.md) · [exact complete-export P/Q8 comparison](../reports/DELVERS_S2E07_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md): **1,520 / 22,664 = 6.71% textual disagreement** (**not WER/accuracy**). Full primary 00:00–02:48:24.250, complete Q export parsed and selected Q windows independently checked, **no listening or GM Discord diary/map verification**. Starts with S2E06 Hank Tom death **only in recap**, then live aftermath. Delvers find **enchanted mechanical crab dredgers #2/#3**, use **Evelyn's magical paints with Mack drawing to create working key #2**, and recover **Hank Tom's crab controls/diary**, **Caleb's diary** and **Ambermoor's diary**. Journals say **three fragile chaos gems**, suspicious drinks and **deliberate distilled chaos phage weaponization**; science officer **Neko** becomes subject, worker **Destin** allegedly green slaad. **Balmer** name tag on adult red slaad who wounds Koh; party kills it (Krandal face maces final), Koh discovers injected moving egg and **physically cuts it out with psychic dagger/hoof-crushes larva**. **Evelyn actually uses Lesser Restoration to clear Church's visible larval infection**; not proof of cure in late-stage transformation. Evelyn pilots **crab #2 underwater** for vehicle **#3 key in Destin's burned house**, then two crabs navigate **underwater cave**; hidden hatch and **Alarm** found, **Koh swims stealthily into laboratory**, Evelyn triggers alarm. **Ambermoor NONLETHALLY knocked unconscious by Koh's psychic blade**, bound/gagged in **Sultan's Sash** and captured; he does **not** die. **Neko-labelled black slaad sedated in glass tank**, Evelyn's Lesser Restoration **has no effect**, then Evelyn **stabs creature dead**. **Four reagent samples (red, blue, green, black) kept in Ambermoor briefcase in Koh's Bag of Holding**; chaos gems processed/dissolved, none recovered intact. Two large slaadi **still missing** when leaving island; **Poppin' Slaads is not conclusively fulfilled**. Herman Snips signals Gil; **three Delvers plus captive/evidence stop at Krandal's farm**, **Mack/cured Church continue by ferry to Atomer guild**. **NO guild report, handoff, payment or dragon hunt yet**; dragon-slayer future guest is host teaser. **Next Delvers S2E08 — Golden Potato Sword**, source inventory confirms P/Q; **unresearched**. Listen/check diary source artwork, red-blue transmission, crab custody, final slaad status and spells.

**S2E06 — Frog Man Cometh researched (ASR-provisional):** [dossier](episodes/S2E06.md) · [full P/Q8 comparison](../reports/DELVERS_S2E06_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md), **1,389 / 21,197 = 6.55% exact textual disagreement** (**not WER/accuracy**). Both complete source exports parsed; complete Parakeet narrated content read through **02:36:12.690**, selected independent Qwen scenes rechecked; no audio listening. **Koh fully uncovers hidden map** under Withers painting and privately copies it: **Black Basilica, roper brood, hook-horror nest, lakebed door and uncertain device/Umbral Flight terminology**. **Krandal hides the heist gems in tower wall and cash under boulder east of farm**; his animated minotaur skull reports unverified fishman watching. **Cassius/Carrie debrief actually happens**: Koh hands over assembled music box, parchment, old ledger/anatomy book, smashed kuo-toa summoner staff/bullywug shaman bell pants, black vials, Hat of Mending, black mirror and mapped information; **Krandal keeps Charlatan's Dice/Candle of the Deep**, can keep but conceal **stolen Cloak of Protection**. **Koh claims freeing Fern initiated Withers house fire**; Withers has hired **Wildfire/Broscale family** to investigate items; **Evelyn's Blackwood surname known by elemental**. Carrie connects **Khalazar/Kalizar** title list to map phrase **“rise again”**, reports older slime can dehydrate to **black sand/water** and offers to restore/read evidence—**not completed**. Koh tells Cassius/Carrie about wife and rejected telepathic contact; potential **Rianu Keeves mental test speculative**, not performed. Cassius asks them to lay low, proposes **possible later unpaid favor**, and they accept **Poppin' Slaads at Gemholm**. Six-hour merfolk **Gil/Gilkeel** ferry with crab **Herman Snips**. At sandbar, frightened **Mack** and injured **Church** describe **red-slaad implanted tadpoles**, **blue-slaad transformations**, missing workers and deliberate boat burning to prevent outbreak. **Caleb dead** with burst chest, tiny larva **killed by Church**, and **Church admits red-slaad scratch two days earlier**, no confirmed immunity. **Hank Tom's transformed red slaad form lethally struck by Evelyn**, Koh's dagger had injured it, Krandal transforms **Staff of Python** to nonlethally obstruct and asks to question; message **not relayed**. Creature apparently says **“thank you”** before death (text-only, meaning unconfirmed). **Cutoff: tide coming in and offshore shadows visible; adult slaads not yet fought**. **Next bounded Delvers S2E07 — The Devils Eggs**, available in [inventory](SOURCE_INVENTORY.md), unresearched. Key listening tasks: map proper names, Khalazar phrase, staff/ledger custody, Church's infection, transformed victim's final words/possibility of rescue.

**S2E05 — Shut up, Fruit Loops! researched (ASR-provisional):** [dossier](episodes/S2E05.md) · [full P/Q8 comparison](../reports/DELVERS_S2E05_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md), **1,321 / 19,669 = 6.72% exact textual disagreement** (**not WER or verified accuracy**). Full primary through 02:22:38.650; Qwen full parsed and selected windows independently checked; no audio. Following S2E04, **Withers Estate now observed burning**, **actual fire origin unresolved**. Shrugs exits by smoke bomb; Koh keeps both bagged proceeds and leaves chalk route markers to Brotherhood sewer hideout; satyrs use **cockatrice egg hair setting**. **21 jade works unbagged vs 23 stolen last episode** (count discrepancy). Brotherhood claims jade and settles **15,000 gp value per character**; Krandal takes **7,800 gold plus remaining 7,200 value in mixed gems** and later **5,000 gold** from Evelyn's refused share; Koh also gets 5,000 extra; Evelyn buys a **5,000-gp Bag of Holding** and refuses remaining 10,000 (separate suggested 6k payment not demonstrated). **Koh covertly retains other bag** with clue book, concealed-map painting and black mirror; **music box fitted with stone disc triggers Swiftclef headache**; Krandal obtains **Charlatan's Dice, Candle of the Deep and Cloak of Protection**. **Withers portrait conceals partially revealed map**; goo-related vials and book about brain/voice anatomy, older elvish name **Calzar/Kalzar?**, and **Withers-financed guild assignments including a Broscale farm-cave mission** all need verification. Nasty gives Koh **signal pan flute**; **no use yet**. Party exits about 04:00 and **postpones Cassius reporting until after a day off**; **no guild debrief played**. **Next bounded Delvers episode: S2E06 — Frog Man Cometh**, available in [inventory](SOURCE_INVENTORY.md), **unresearched**. Listening priorities: estate fire origin, 21/23 jade, book title/name, settlement exact price, hidden-map content, item custody and signal flute.

**S2E04 — Cover The Faces of Maces now researched (ASR-provisional):** [dossier](episodes/S2E04.md) · [exact P/Q8 comparison](../reports/DELVERS_S2E04_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md), **2,105 / 24,028 = 8.76%** textual disagreement (**not WER/accuracy**). Withers Estate **midnight burglary ACTUALLY played through escape**, guest **Shrugs (Brian Dunaway)**; **Koh Psychic Whispers links only Nasty, Shrugs, Evelyn, not Krandal**, newly fitted Boots of Elvenkind used. **Krandal casts two Silence scrolls** enabling **first underground door and final vault dynamite breaches**, **Evelyn carries third unused**. Basement former **Enzo prison** with **dried kuo-toa corpse**; capital-letter clue **CROP** opens first secret door. **Fire guardian Fern Fueler shrunk but alive by Krandal's 20 gallons water**, **water guardian Dewey Liquis alive**, **air guardian Gale alive (Shrugs temporarily at 0 HP, revived by Krandal Preserve Life)**; keys earned by combats, **earth lift Slate Cortez** solved using **coat** riddle/key without combat. **Koh actually throws two psychic knives** (new Snake Island recollection); **Krandal actually animates Staff of Python into giant snake** (unlike S2E03). **Krandal discreetly pockets ~500-gp aquamarine**; Shrugs takes **music box missing record and dried kuo-toa toe**. **Koh steals 23 portable jade objects** from museum (large sculptures remain); servant sees **Shrugs disguised as coat pile**, reports “coat monster/thieves”. Downstairs, **Evelyn physically smashes familiar conch-topped staff and bell-trousers**, Koh bags pieces; **staff may resemble S1E11 fish ritual staff but identity NOT confirmed**. **Koh and Shrugs load two borrowed Bags of Holding with gems, unknown black-liquid vials and smaller magical-looking items**, possible music-box disc not securely identified. **Four versus six final dynamite sticks described inconsistently**. **All four adventurers ESCAPE in Allspice's cart**, Withers arrives after; **no handoff, valuation, proof of Withers misconduct or money payout**. Koh's proposed **Fern burns mansion** is only suggestion, not played fire. **Next bounded Delvers research S2E05 — Shut up, Fruit Loops!**, unresearched.

**S2E03 — Pokey Stick Junior — ASR-provisional dossier saved:** [dossier](episodes/S2E03.md) · [full P/Q8 exact report](../reports/DELVERS_S2E03_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md), **1,427 / 19,062 = 7.49%** textual disagreement, **not WER**. **All-bronze bulette defeated** in Atomer finance district; **450 gp operation fee stated, group vs each unclear**; Koh finds **recently used, strapped stone slab in subterranean Withers chamber** exposed by bulette, **locked door unopened**, reports to Cassius; Withers' denial of knowledge **disputed, not disproved**. **Koh demonstrates dual psychic-blade hits**, Krandal strikes bulette eye with staff, Evelyn rides it as it dies. **Krandal actually plants potatoes, renovates irrigation by hand and mounts talking minotaur skull as scarecrow; “Spud Buds” tentative name, not finished farm**. **Evelyn selects school courses, Bronze Ball next week, classes in two**. Chuck/Nasty **recruits Koh** to coordinate psychic communication for projected Withers jade heist, claims 750-gp debt and 10k–20k gross haul **neither paid**. **“Suis Sac” reversed spells CASSIUS, and Cassius CONFIRMS financing the off-books Brotherhood operation** to investigate suspected Withers artifact/Skull Keep wrongdoing. **Evelyn explicitly corrects family surname to *Blackwood* singular** rather than earlier S2E01 Blackwater ASR and tells Koh/Krandal she is only daughter. Team aliases **Flatfoot Skippy, Cobra Commander, Long Jump Jenny**; guild **loans Boots of Elvenkind**, Koh hoof modification **pending**. **9:30 p.m. infiltration only planned; episode ends as unnamed elf arrives at guild**, no mansion entry. **S2E04 researched separately; current next S2E05 — Shut up, Fruit Loops!**.

**S2E02 — Why Palor When you Can Pay Later now researched (ASR-provisional):** [dossier](episodes/S2E02.md) · [full P/Q8 report](../reports/DELVERS_S2E02_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md) (**1,835 / 24,426 = 7.51% exact textual disagreement**, not WER). **Wight Wedding actually played**: guest **Great Daufante/Daufonte** and zombie Connor; Koh recognizes ability to wield **two psychic blades** through a Snake Island flashback; Evelyn **actually summons once-monthly Goat of Travail** to save ceremony after 20 doves found dead; Krandal slays animated knife-bearing duck and collects **220 gp-equivalent festival gold/gems**. Senior Mr. Goodwine **confesses under Charm Person to beating/hanging grandfather Hooper fifteen years earlier, leaving corpse unburied**; **wight on walking tree defeated**, corpse **buried by Goodwine assisted by Connor**. Guest retrieves **Deck of Many Things**, **does not draw** and **leaves with deck, forfeiting fee/share to three Delvers**; exact guild payout split not proven. **Black sludge on tree roots** and other moving sludge footprints unexplained; Koh right-hand trophy near body inferred, requires audio. **Wedding successfully celebrated. Follow-up S2E03 researched separately; current next archive S2E04 — Cover The Faces of Maces**.

**Season Two premiere S2E01 — Very Snakey now researched (ASR provisional):** [Dossier](episodes/S2E01.md) · [full comparison](../reports/DELVERS_S2E01_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md), **1,749 / 22,859 = 7.65% inter-ASR textual disagreement**, not WER/accuracy. **Return after two forgotten Snake Island weeks, 3,000 gp group payment, new snake gear; old deed physically delivered; Koh confronts Cloven Brotherhood; Evelyn's Blackwater parents and divine mark revealed; sleeping Rianu whispers “Kalizar” but does not wake; sea hag killed at ruined Potato Grove, minotaur's talking skull buried alive; “White Wedding” accepted for tomorrow at 530 gp, not played.** Season One still ends at S1E12; S2E00 remains an in-universe earlier cutaway despite archive label. **Follow-ups S2E02/S2E03 researched separately; current next archive S2E04 — Cover The Faces of Maces**. Exact paths are in [source inventory](SOURCE_INVENTORY.md). [S1E11 dossier](episodes/S1E11.md) and [P/Q8 report](../reports/DELVERS_S1E11_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md) record **8.39% exact ordered textual disagreement, not WER/accuracy**. **Water Breathing ends only after all Delvers surface alive**; party discovers a **Dawnless Dunes wall slit, black sludge sample, Wand of Secrets, quarter geared disc, fog bottle**, plus unopened **toothed stone gate**. Koh kills an unnamed **floating brain-beaked tentacled creature**; its beak halves become makeshift Krandal pauldrons. The trader **Glepo Ma hands fish ritualist's staff to threatening darkmantle-hatted rider**, who heads toward the bullywugs and orders two accomplices to ambush/rob the Delvers. Koh knocks out robed caster nonlethally; Krandal's **spectral face mace** drops huge armored fighter, whose altered face reveals **Broadside's appearance**. **Three prisoners alive** (wizard, robed caster, armored fighter); trader **actually swims west to warn bullywugs**, but message delivery is **not observed**. Koh takes **gear crank and ~1,000 gp bag** in compensation; the fish staff goes with fleeing rider. **Final cutoff: Delvers leave kuo-toa village on horses toward guild with prisoners, but DO NOT arrive.** No cult/god motives or guild-betrayal identities independently proven.

**April 2021 bonus — mostly Delvers retrospective (no played-source advancement):** [BONUS-2021-04 dossier](../episodes/BONUS-2021-04.md) · [exact P/Q8 report](../reports/BONUS_2021_04_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md) (**479 / 7,067 = 6.78% textual disagreement**, not WER). Jon says **Koh's guild application reveals his full name despite hopes to hide adventuring from aristocratic family**; Scott/Kristen describe changes to Krandal's faith/potato aims and Evelyn's age/name/school concept. **GM confirms earlier cockatrice scar healed, Skull Keep upland lake belongs to larger kuo-toa water system, and common pit traps descend farther**, plus **undiscovered Skull Keep basement/alchemy lab** and **unrecovered first-grick-ruin tablet**; neither missed clue becomes played PC knowledge. Cast says **Broadside's Greatsword of Wounding was returned** after the trust decision; exact moment unverified. **12-episode season design** is a pacing policy, not rule of character history. Future setting kits, Bronze Ball and Snake Island described prospectively. Next monthly bonus **2021-05**, P/Q8 existence confirmed; **next Delvers archive is now S2E03 — Pokey Stick Junior (S2E01/S2E02 researched)**; no listening or new story scene.

**S2E00 — Cassius at the Guild:** [Dossier](episodes/S2E00.md) · [P/Q8 report](../reports/DELVERS_S2E00_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md) (**80 / 1,451 = 5.51%** textual disagreement, not accuracy). A **10–11-minute narrated fictional cutaway**, **not regular party play or an out-of-game bonus**. Cassius and Carrie attend **Dungeon Guild Academy's Radiant Lance Theatre** while the Delvers are in the kuo-toa village. Cassius requests **gold-league aid against the Underdark**, carries Carrie's evidence (horn and psychic shafts), argues against dismissive board and unexpectedly voices doubts about Krandal, Koh and Evelyn. **Board refuses new funding, recommends Bronze Ball/Withers donors and announces Selenar Everbloom's inspection**; duo set out home by coach. **Before S1E12** in-story; separate last 22 seconds/Qwen “Oh” audio verification queued. Archive **S2E00 retained** and [guild academy](world/places/dungeon-guild-academy.md) / [Cassius](world/characters/cassius.md) documented. No new party knowledge is inferred.

**Season-one finale S1E12 — End Friends:** [Dossier](episodes/S1E12.md) · [exact Parakeet/Qwen report](../reports/DELVERS_S1E12_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md) (**8.22% textual disagreement; not WER**). **Rest/armor re-equipping is played before the road journey**; Boonefellow brings **all three captives** to guild while the three Delvers pursue kidnapped Faelan. **Broadside and Cheet** questioned under Zone of Truth; guild researcher **Marek/Merrick** attempting **midnight Noble Hollow high-elf sacrifice and beast summoning**. Broadside helps rescue, **Evelyn interrupts rite nonlethally**, matching gear-disc **shatters**. Fall exposes **roper breeding piercers**; **Evelyn kills roper**, **Faelan and Norman healed alive**, one unnamed cultist swallowed. Postbattle debrief **clears Delvers, Broadside, Solburn**, sends **Marek toward trial and Cheet toward rehabilitation** (future administration). No extra guild cash, but **old farmland tower deed promised to Krandal**; **Snake Island job only offered** by gold-and-snakes-bearing emissary in final scene. **First story arc and season one end here**, but Dunes, wife, sleeping elves and ancient ruins remain unresolved. [First arc narrative](narrative/SEASON_ONE_ARC.md).

**Earlier S1E10 context:** [S1E10 dossier](episodes/S1E10.md) and [P/Q8 report](../reports/DELVERS_S1E10_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md) record **8.27%** exact word disagreement, not accuracy. Koh **contacts his unconscious wife in a dune/drone vision** and bottles physically manifest black sand; Krandal's sleeping-elf code is tentatively a **funeral dirge**. Guild sends the party **peacefully** to freshwater kuo-toa village, whose people treat telepathic Koh as a god. In a flooded repeated-layout ruin, **Krandal puts on a Ring of Protection** and the group **subdues a staff-wielding fish ritualist alive**. He claims a god sleeps in the **Dunes**. **At cutoff, restrained captive is on Krandal's back, still below the lake; the surface return and trader judgment are NOT played**. Potions of Water Breathing were consumed. See new dossier for exact custody, hazards, uncertain names and one-hour timing.

**Earlier S1E09 context:** [S1E09 dossier](episodes/S1E09.md) and [ASR comparison](../reports/DELVERS_S1E09_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md) document **6.98%** exact P/Q word disagreement. In S1E09, **Evelyn destroys the gelatinous cube**, Koh **kills a hook horror** while another survives, and trophies including **Horn of Blasting** are submitted to Carrie. The Delvers receive **300 gp each**, recover Koh's magical sash, investigate a **second shaft beneath Pelor's main altar** with troubling drone and unresponsive elves, and purchase equipment including **Evelyn's Goat of Travail**. The **kuo-toa mission is selected but not played**; **level four is explicitly announced by GM for next episode**. Details, purchase/delivery uncertainty and listening windows are tracked in the dossier.

**Prior S1E08 context:** [S1E08 dossier](episodes/S1E08.md) and [ASR comparison](../reports/DELVERS_S1E08_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md) document **8.30% P/Q disagreement**. The southwestern well was descended, a natural cave breach found, and its passage **sealed with rocks/concrete** in cooperation with First Sons Brotherhood. An ancient ruin opened **physically into Pelor's temple**, damaging its floor. At S1E08 cutoff six adventurers have discovered a **gelatinous cube** in deeper, still-explorable caverns; **no ensuing combat**, no proved water safety, and Koh's climbing sash **not yet retrieved**. Spellings of guild companions and item custody remain provisional.

**Earlier S1E07 context:** [S1E07 dossier](episodes/S1E07.md) and [ASR comparison](../reports/DELVERS_S1E07_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md) document **7.05% P/Q disagreement**. S1E07 ends with an **uninspected southwestern well**, Brigand Patrol on watch, and the Delvers heading back with **unused concrete**. Koh's hilt-free psychic blade, Wildfire/Brom Broscale, Margaret's bag, the guild's unverified ecological hypotheses and corrected item custody are all documented in that dossier. The completed [S1E06 dossier](episodes/S1E06.md) and [ASR comparison](../reports/DELVERS_S1E06_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md) report **1,475 / 23,887 = 6.17%** ordered inter-ASR word disagreement, **not accuracy**. No audio listened.

**S1E06 cutoff:** All three have **unnumbered bronze badges** (S1E05 only promised the ceremony), **Koh holds one shared guild library key**. The Darkest Delvers complete **Skull Keep**, Koh kills its flameskull with Soul Knife and bags **two orange garnets** after **Evelyn applies one of two holy-water jars**. Servants stop moving; **Enzo's mirror dims without verified destruction**. Paid guild contract stated as 350 gold, later **about 400 bonus gold** after antique damage (final per-person accounting open). **XP off-air; no level-up demonstrated**. Enzo's **Dawnless Dunes** warning is NPC testimony, not verified cosmology. **Evelyn reveals she seeks someone**, identity undisclosed; Koh questions Enzo about a paralytic condition but does not name his wife. See [Skull Keep profile](world/places/skull-keep.md), [Enzo](world/characters/enzo-vanderbuck-withers.md) and [consistency ledger](world/CONSISTENCY_LEDGER.md).

**Remaining specific checks:** `DEL-S1E06-001–009` in [dossier](episodes/S1E06.md): client and necromancer spellings, `Dawnless Dunes` interpretation/handout, holy-water counting, S1E05 equipment pickup, damaged antiques and bonus units, failed adventurers, and audio clock alignment. Old S1E03 mislabeled sources remain flagged separately; do not change source filenames.

